The fresh mutation passed the non-vacuity gate exactly as required: it parsed and dry-ran successfully, then exited 1 with `WarnStuckClaimState` at the result obligation, showing actual `"b"` against the false empty-string target. The exhaustive inventory now covers 698 rules, 228 syntax declarations, every context/configuration, all function/total/priority/simplification attributes, and every opaque symbol; no proof-local operational bridge or oracle exists. I’m writing the final seven-stage review and trust ledger now.
